**Read:** [Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle](../sources/Physical-Geology-Earle.lingua#r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX), the complete book and exercises; [Introduction to Historical Geology — Estrada and contributing authors](../sources/Introduction-to-Historical-Geology.lingua#r_1JKSSECEDW0M9QG30TJ1D9KHZD), the complete book; [Geodiversidade do Brasil — Cassio Roberto da Silva and contributors](../sources/Geodiversidade-do-Brasil.lingua#r_2ZQN8TT3KZYS9MCFGZV5A1V682), the complete book; [Geodiversidade do estado do Rio Grande do Sul — Viero and Silva](../sources/Geodiversidade-Rio-Grande-do-Sul.lingua#r_177DN2HQXX9X7QQB6TNSS3RD3N), the complete regional volume; [Laboratory Manual for Introductory Geology — Deline, Harris, and Tefend](../sources/Introductory-Geology-Laboratory-Manual.lingua#r_7G68RZ432EQWTB84DSVJ4JCZ2Z), the complete manual; [Introduction to Geology — Perron and Jagoutz, MIT 12.001](../sources/MIT-Introduction-to-Geology.lingua#r_423FFVY46CGEN2F2263F95KX6N), the full published course sequence; [Geological Structures: a Practical Introduction — Waldron and Snyder](../sources/Geological-Structures-Waldron-Snyder.lingua#r_2RC4KMK6ADFX90708NZH2F6RRW), the complete book and all ten labs.

Read all 22 chapters of Physical Geology, the complete Introduction to Historical Geology, and all of Geodiversidade do Brasil. Work their exercises and preserve explanations for errors or revised interpretations. Read the whole Rio Grande do Sul volume as a sustained regional case, comparing it with the western Canadian chapter and actual map legends.

Complete the entire introductory laboratory manual and MIT 12.001's published notes/labs/exercises, matching concepts where the course assigns a commercial textbook. Read the full Geological Structures book and perform its ten labs. The original numerical plane is one small inspectable exercise, not a replacement for orientation, mapping, specimen, section, and structural work.

Use appropriate supervised specimen, instrument, microscopy, and field work to demonstrate practical abilities where the exercises call for them. Published images and virtual exercises can establish interpretation skills but cannot alone demonstrate measuring an orientation, identifying a specimen under real conditions, or managing a field observation programme. State what was actually done.

**Work:** produce an integrated account of one region's materials, structures, chronology, landscapes, and water, with original diagrams and quantitative checks. Defend interpretations against alternatives and connect each claim with observations or source passages. Revisit earlier explanations as later reading exposes assumptions.

These are learning demands, not new software gates or authoring forms. Begin freely at any Record; sustained completion means being able to perform and explain the work rather than collecting reading titles. The following studies deepen this foundation into independent practical and academic investigation.

**Continue:** [Carry out a sustained mapping study from question to revised geological model](Independent-mapping-and-field-evidence-study.lingua#r_5ZC4N7CSG8RZF5ZT177EHCFQYR).

**Return:** [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06).
